   "body": "**Adversarial review (fable, cloud/review-brows-fable): APPROVE** — head 3c486f67\n\nThe three requested checks pass. One non-blocking finding.\n\n1. **Low** — `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md:322`. The sentence still reads as the full list of (b) rows that merged code ships, but it is only the 2026-11-01 list minus the reclassified rows. Other `b` rows are merged too: GAP-085 (LOT-085, #458; the next bullet itself says it \"ports the feature\") and GAP-229 (#577, LOT-122 #589) for certain; by merged lot title also 028/029/034 (LOT-125, #542), 097 (LOT-088, #557), 166 (LOT-157, #745), 209 (LOT-118, #640), 202 (LOT-163, #717). Scenario: a reader counting what (b) work is left takes six rows as shipped and the other 31 as not. Fix: either complete the list, or word it as non-exhaustive and dated (\"among them, as of 2026-11-01: …\"). Pre-existing, so it can be a follow-up; the commit title \"refresh the list\" overstates what was done.\n\n**Verified**\n- Diff: one line changed, one file; `git diff --check` clean.\n- 008, 009, 051, 060, 092, 163: H.1 = `b` in their rows (lines 32, 33, 74, 83, 118, 190) and in the `b` tally row.\n- Their work is merged on `dev-swift`: #540 merged 2026-11-07 as dc38ffb9 (008); specs of LOT-081, 083, 084, 087, 167, 170, 063 present; #594-related, #427 (#744) and #431 (#955) commits found.\n- 020, 022: `a` in row and tally. 214: `a`; 212: `a·master`. Both are type `same`, so correctly absent from the tally (it covers only `ported with changes`, `UX change`, `new`).\n- Scripted cross-check of all 133 tally rows against the H.1 column: no mismatch, counts 49/10/8/29/37 exact.\n- No dropped row should stay: the four removed are no longer (b).\n\nNot run: the Docs consistency CI check (no local entry point found); only commit titles, not behaviour, for the rows of finding 1 other than 085 and 229.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
